Welcome to your first home cooking class! Today, we are mastering the most classic dish in Chinese home cooking: the Tomato and Egg Stir-fry. While it seems simple, it is a perfect exercise in heat control and ingredient texture. 

Before we begin, take a look at our goal: a plate of bright red, glossy, and perfectly balanced tomato and egg stir-fry.

<image1>

### Step 1: Prepare Your Supplies
As the saying goes, "To do a good job, one must first sharpen one's tools." For beginners, the biggest mistake is searching for ingredients while the pan is already smoking. Arrange the following on your countertop: two fully ripe tomatoes (the riper they are, the more juice they will release), two fresh eggs, salt, cooking oil, and a small dish of white sugar. You will also need a sharp knife, a cutting board, a bowl, and a non-stick pan.

<image2>

### Step 2: Process the Ingredients
Wash the tomatoes and cut them into large chunks. Do not cut them too finely; keeping some chunks allows them to maintain their shape and release juice more slowly. Crack the eggs into a bowl and add a small spoonful of salt. The salt helps break down the protein structure, making the eggs fluffier. Whisk or stir thoroughly until the egg whites and yolks are fully blended into a uniform, golden liquid.

<image3>

### Step 3: Sauté the Eggs
Place your non-stick pan on the burner and turn on the heat. When the pan is warm, pour in an appropriate amount of oil. When the oil shows slight ripples or a faint wisp of smoke, pour in the beaten eggs. You will hear a pleasant sizzling sound. Use your spatula to quickly push and spread the egg liquid from the edges toward the center until it solidifies into a golden, fluffy mass.

<image4>

### Step 4: Sauté the Tomatoes
Once the eggs are about 80% set—meaning they are still slightly moist and tender in the middle—use the spatula to push them to one side of the pan. This leaves a small amount of oil in the center. Add the tomato chunks now. You will see them soften quickly. Use the spatula to gently press down on the tomatoes to help break the skin and accelerate the release of the red juice.

<image5>

### Step 5: Create the Sauce
When the tomatoes have softened and released a significant amount of juice, pour in half a bowl of water. The water will turn red as it mixes with the tomato juice. Add a small spoonful of sugar; this enhances the freshness and helps the sauce thicken. Turn the heat to high and stir-fry quickly until the water and tomato juice boil vigorously into a thick, bright red sauce.

<image6>

### Step 6: Final Mix and Serve
Turn the heat to low and mix the eggs back into the sauce. The goal is to let the eggs absorb the thickened tomato sauce. Stir-fry gently until every piece of egg is coated in a shiny red glaze. When the sauce has reduced to a thick consistency and clings to the ingredients, turn off the heat. Your perfect Tomato and Egg Stir-fry is ready to serve!

